{"data":{"updated_timestamp":"25/09/2026 13:46:08","profile":{"player_id":"18543","last_updated":"25/09/2026 13:46","fullname":"Mohammad Ishaq Shirzad","short_display_name":"M Ishaq","name":"Mohammad Ishaq","gender":"M","dob":"01/02/2005","date_of_death":null,"place_birth":"Afghanistan","nationality_id":"262","nationality":"Afghanistan","nationality_short_code":"AFG","nick_name":"Ishaq Rahimi","player_skill":{"id":"4","text":"Wicket Keeper","role":"Wicket Keeper"},"batting_style":{"id":"1","text":"Right Handed"},"bowling_style":{"id":"","text":"-"},"writeup":"<p>Mohammad Ishaq, born on February 1st, 2005, in Nangarhar, Afghanistan, is a talented right-handed wicketkeeper-batter. He showcased his cricketing prowess by making his first-class debut for Speen Ghar Region during the 2018 Ahmad Shah Abdali 4-day Tournament on April 15, 2018. Continuing his promising journey, he marked his List A debut for the same team in the 2018 Ghazi Amanullah Khan Regional One-Day Tournament on July 25, 2018. In December 2019, Ishaq's talents earned him a spot in Afghanistan's squad for the 2020 Under-19 Cricket World Cup. He further solidified his presence on the international stage by representing Afghanistan in the 2022 ICC Under-19 Cricket World Cup held in the West Indies.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nIshaq's transition to senior cricket saw him make his T20 debut against Sri Lanka at Rangiri Dambulla International Stadium on February 21, 2024. In a memorable debut, he remained unbeaten, contributing a crucial 16 runs off just 8 balls, aiding Afghanistan's victory by 3 runs. A significant milestone in his career came with his inclusion in Afghanistan's 15-member squad for the T20 World Cup 2024. This maiden World Cup call was a testament to Ishaq's talent and potential, marking a significant milestone in his cricketing journey.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nOn the league circuit, Ishaq has been a regular in Afghanistan&rsquo;s domestic T20 structure, turning out for Speen Ghar Tigers and later Boost Defenders. While he has not yet featured in overseas franchise leagues, his growing reputation as a steady wicketkeeper-batter suggests those opportunities may not be far away.</p>","relation":null,"social_details":null,"trophy_cabinet":null,"majorteams":{"team":[{"id":"1143","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"1","text":"Afghanistan Under-19"},{"id":"1188","active":"1","is_primary":"true","is_international":"1","text":"Afghanistan"},{"id":"1550","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Afghanistan A"},{"id":"1603","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Speen Ghar Region"},{"id":"1605","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Amo Region"},{"id":"1608","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Amo Sharks"},{"id":"1611","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Kabul Eagles"},{"id":"3092","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Hindukush Strikers"},{"id":"3966","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Maiwand Champions"},{"id":"3967","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Mahipar Stars"}]},"international_debut":{"comp_type_id":"3","comp_type":"T20 International - m","match_id":"239022","match_center":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/matches/239022/sri-lanka-vs-afghanistan","series_id":"6081","series_name":"Afghanistan in Sri Lanka, 3 T20I Series, 2024","match_date":"21/02/2024","for":{"id":"1188","text":"Afghanistan","short_name":"AFG"},"vs":{"id":"8","text":"Sri Lanka","short_name":"SL"},"venue":{"id":"133","text":"Rangiri Dambulla International Stadium, Dambulla"},"batting":{"runs":"16","balls_faced":"8","hundreds":"0","innings":[{"number":"1","runs":"16","balls_faced":"8","hundreds":""}]},"bowling":{"wickets":"","runs_given":"","ball_bowled":"","economy":"","five_wk_hauls":"0","innings":[]},"fielding":{"catches":"1","stumpings":"0","run_outs":"0","innings":[